          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#PlainNotion Plain notion
          %p
            By default, by a
            %em real vector bundle
            over a plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            one means a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+spaces"} real vector spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated
            to an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
            the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
          %p
            This is in contrast notably to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundles"} complex vector bundles
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+vector+bundles"} quaternionic vector bundles
          %h3#InKRTheory In KR-theory
          %p
            In the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KR-theory"} KR-theory
            (“Real K-theory”) and following
            %a{:href => "#Atiyah66"} Atiyah 1966 p. 368
            one considers a more general notion (which subsumes the plain notion above, see Exp.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RealVectorBundlesAsRealVectorBundles"}
            below):
          %p
          #AtiyahRealVectorBundle.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (Atiyah Real vector bundles)
              %br/
              A
              %em Real vector bundle
              (capital “R” for disambiguation) over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Real+space"} Real space
              – namely over
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group+of+order+2"}
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mn 2
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-space"} equivariant space
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ↷
                        %mi X
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ∈
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                        %mi Top
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi Func
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi Top
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\mathbb{Z}_2 \curvearrowright X
                        \\;\in\;
                        \\mathbb{Z}_2 Top
                        \\;=\;
                        Func\big(
                        \\mathbf{B}\mathbb{Z}_2
                        ,\,
                        Top
                        \\big)
                %p
                  hence a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                  equipped with a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
