            %p
          %p
          #ComplexVectorBundlesAsRealBundles.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Similarly to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:RealVectorBundlesOverVaryingBaseSpaces"} (3)
              = succeed "-inclusion" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundles"} complex vector bundles
              over varying base spaces into Real vector bundles over varying bases spaces with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free action
            #eq:RealVectorBundlesOverVaryingBaseSpaces.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                %mo ∫
                              %mrow
                                %mi X
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi Top
                            %mi ℂ
                            %msub
                              %mi Vect
                              %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mo ∼
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                %mo ∫
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi ℤ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mn 2
                                %mo ×
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi ℤ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mn 2
                                %mi Top
                            %msub
                              %mi RealVect
                              %mrow
                                %mi ℤ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mn 2
                                %mo ×
                                %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi E
                              %mo ¯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo ×
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo ×
                            %mi X
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\underset{X \in Top}{\textstyle{\int}}
                    \\mathbb{C}Vect_X
                    \&amp;\xrightarrow{\; \sim \;}&amp;
                    \\underset{
                    (\mathbb{Z}/2 \times X) \in \mathbb{Z}/2 Top
                    }{\textstyle{\int}}
                    RealVect_{\mathbb{Z}/2 \times X}
                    \\\
                    E
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    E &amp; \overline{E}
                    \\\
                    \\big\downarrow
                    \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    \\big\downarrow
                    \&amp;
                    \\big\downarrow
                    \\\
                    X
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\{0\} \times X
                    \&amp;
                    \\{1\} \times X
                    \\,
                    }
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{E}
              denotes the vector bundle with fiber-wise anti-linear structure. However, as is this is not a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+functor"} full functor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ↔
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leftrightarrow 1
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-linear+map"} anti-linear map
            %p
              To make the above into an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
              one can equip the Real vector bundles moreover with involutions which square to -1 – ie.
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structures"} complex structures
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
              to Real vector bundles! – and require the maps to respect these further involutions. Then the functor which takes a “Real vector bundle with complex structure” over a free
              = succeed "-space" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} +\mathrm{i}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eigenvalue"} eigenvalue
              bundle (of the internal complex structure), constitutes an equivalence with complex vector bundles.
            %p In this sense the term “Real vector bundle” is quite appropriate.
